https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHC8lYBditA  (Capo 0) (MC0)

TIP:  The intro begins with a quick two-count before the first (D).  So form (D) and pick the 2nd string, then the 1st string, and strum (D).

FUN FACT:  Written by Janis Gill (one half of Sweethearts of the Rodeo, who also perform the song) and their father John, the song is somewhat tongue-in-cheek as, while there is an Innisfree in Ireland, it’s a small uninhabited island in County Sligo.  No inn exists.  


